-- title:
--   Rule (3.6) gives $(1+2\gamma_k\mu_B)/\gamma_k^2 = (1-2\gamma_{k+1}\mu_C\eta)/\gamma_{k+1}^2$
-- statement:
--   Let $\mu_B \ge 0$, $\mu_C > 0$, $\eta \in (0,1)$ and $\gamma_0 > 0$, and let $(\gamma_k)_{k \ge 0}$ be generated by the stepsize rule (3.6). Then for every $k \ge 0$
--   $$\frac{1 + 2\gamma_k\mu_B}{\gamma_k^2} = \frac{1 - 2\gamma_{k+1}\mu_C\eta}{\gamma_{k+1}^2}.$$
--
--   This identity is what the rule (3.6) is designed for: it matches the coefficient of $\|x_B^{k+1} - x^*\|^2$ on the left of (3.9), divided by $\gamma_k^2$, with the coefficient of $\|x_B^{k+1} - x^*\|^2$ on the right of (3.9) at the next step, divided by $\gamma_{k+1}^2$, so that (3.9) telescopes.
-- source:
--   Davis and Yin, A Three-Operator Splitting Scheme and its Optimization Applications, Set-Valued Var. Anal. 25 (2017), https://doi.org/10.1007/s11228-017-0421-z, p. 845, Section 3.3, proof of Theorem 3.3, Part 1 (unnumbered display)

import Mathlib
import Definitions.Def_ThreeOpSplitting_Accel_Stepsizes

open Filter Topology

namespace ThreeOpSplitting.Accel

/-- Proof of Theorem 3.3, Part 1 (p. 845): the rule (3.6) ensures
`(1 + 2γ_kμ_B)/γ_k² = (1 - 2γ_{k+1}μ_Cη)/γ_{k+1}²` for all `k ≥ 0`. -/
theorem stepsize_identity_part1 (μB μC η γ0 : ℝ)
    (hμB : 0 ≤ μB) (hμC : 0 < μC) (hη0 : 0 < η) (hη1 : η < 1) (hγ0 : 0 < γ0) (k : ℕ) :
    (1 + 2 * stepsPart1 μB μC η γ0 k * μB) / stepsPart1 μB μC η γ0 k ^ 2
      = (1 - 2 * stepsPart1 μB μC η γ0 (k + 1) * μC * η) / stepsPart1 μB μC η γ0 (k + 1) ^ 2 := by sorry

end ThreeOpSplitting.Accel
